NONE","body":"PR submitted: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/325\n\nReady for review. The script has been tested on a real repo with 154 commits. Includes README and SKILL.md.","createdAt":"2026-03-30T18:55:41Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4157396791","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M7328WJ","author":{"login":"RavMonSOL"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-30T21:45:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4158375305","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M7348Gk","author":{"login":"JuanM94"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nSubmitted PR #329 — complete changelog generator with SKILL.md, bash script, and README. Tested with conventional commits and git tags.","createdAt":"2026-03-31T00:00:05Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4158898596","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M737SVx","author":{"login":"willkhinz"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I've got a fix coming. I am working on a fix for this and will open a PR shortly.","createdAt":"2026-03-31T02:58:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4159513969","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M738XZY","author":{"login":"yuliuyi717-ux"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\\n\\nImplemented this and opened a PR with the changelog skill, `changelog.sh`, tests, and a sample generated changelog from a real repo.","createdAt":"2026-03-31T04:29:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4159796824","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M739BY4","author":{"login":"1150654748m-dev"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-31T05:21:29Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4159968824","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M739fGh","author":{"login":"zlplzp123wyt"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nSubmitted PR #340 with the changelog generation skill. Tested on deer-flow repo (1750 commits correctly categorized).","createdAt":"2026-03-31T05:49:01Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4160090529","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73_Cay","author":{"login":"BetsyMalthus"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nI've built a complete CHANGELOG generator skill with both bash wrapper and Python implementation. Features: auto-categorization (Added/Fixed/Changed/Removed), tag detection, multiple output formats (Markdown/JSON/Text), and full Claude Code skill integration. PR incoming shortly.","createdAt":"2026-03-31T07:23:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4160497330","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73_y0F","author":{"login":"BetsyMalthus"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nI've built a complete Claude Code skill for generating structured CHANGELOG from git history.\n\n✅ **Features**\n- Full SKILL.md with Claude Code integration\n- Python script with intelligent commit categorization\n- Bash wrapper script (changelog.sh) as required\n- Auto-categorizes into Added/Fixed/Changed/Removed\n- Tested on real repository\n- 3-step setup in README\n\n✅ **Deliverables ready**:\n- SKILL.md (Claude Code skill definition)\n- scripts/generate_changelog.py (core implementation)\n- changelog.sh (bash wrapper)\n- README.md (3-step setup)\n- Sample CHANGELOG output from real repo\n\nPR incoming shortly with complete implementation!","createdAt":"2026-03-31T08:03:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4160695557","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M74AAa1","author":{"login":"BetsyMalthus"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"✅ **PR submitted**: #344\n\nComplete CHANGELOG generator skill with all 7 acceptance criteria met:\n\n1. ✅ Works via `/generate-changelog` command (Claude Code skill)\n2. ✅ Works via `bash changelog.sh` (bash wrapper)\n3. ✅ Fetches commits since last git tag\n4. ✅ Auto-categorizes into Added/Fixed/Changed/Removed\n5. ✅ Outputs properly formatted CHANGELOG.md\n6. ✅ Tested on real repo (sample output included)\n7. ✅ README with 3-step setup\n\n**Files included**:\n- `SKILL.md` - Full Claude Code skill definition\n- `scripts/generate_changelog.py` - Core Python implementation\n- `changelog.sh` - Bash wrapper (as required)\n- `README.md` - 3-step setup instructions\n- `TEST_CHANGELOG.md` - Sample output from real repository\n\nReady for review and merge! 🚀","createdAt":"2026-03-31T08:12:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4160751285","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M74B037","author":{"login":"qq2825961339"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"\n### 🚀 Solution: Automated CHANGELOG Generator\n\nI've created a production-ready Python script that generates structured CHANGELOG files from Git history.\n\n#### 📦 Deliverable\n**Script File**: `generate_changelog.py` (full code below)\n\n#### ⚙️ Features\n- **Multiple Formats**: Supports Markdown, JSON, and Plain Text output.\n- **Conventional Commits**: Automatically categorizes commits (Features, Bug Fixes, Docs, etc.).\n- **Single File**: No external dependencies, just `python generate_changelog.py`.\n- **Customizable**: Configurable commit limit and output path.\n\n#### 🛠️ Usage\n```bash\n# Generate Markdown CHANGELOG\npython generate_changelog.py --format markdown --output CHANGELOG.md\n\n# Generate JSON\npython generate_changelog.py --format json --output changelog.json\n\n# Limit to last 50 commits\npython generate_changelog.py --limit 50\n```\n\n#### 📄 Example Output (Markdown)\n```markdown\n# Changelog\n\n## [2026-03-31]\n- **Features**: Add user authentication module ([`a1b2c3d`](https://github.com/owner/repo/commit/a1b2c3d)) - @dev\n- **Bug Fixes**: Fix login timeout issue ([`e4f5g6h`](https://github.com/owner/repo/commit/e4f5g6h)) - @dev\n```\n\n#### 📄 Full Script Code\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nGenerate a structured CHANGELOG.md from Git history.\nUsage: python generate_changelog.py [--format markdown|json|text] [--output CHANGELOG.md]\n\"\"\"\n\nimport subprocess\nimport json\nimport re\nimport argparse\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import List, Dict\n\ndef get_git_log(limit: int = 100) -> List[Dict]:\n    \"\"\"Fetch git log with structured data\"\"\"\n    cmd = [\n        \"git\", \"log\", f\"-{limit}\", \"--pretty=format:%H|%an|%ae|%ad|%s\",\n        \"--date=short\"\n    ]\n    result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n    \n    entries = []\n    for line in result.stdout.splitlines():\n        if not line:\n            continue\n        parts = line.split(\"|\")\n        if len(parts) >= 5:\n            entries.append({\n                \"hash\": parts[0],\n                \"author\": parts[1],\n                \"email\": parts[2],\n                \"date\": parts[3],\n                \"message\": parts[4]\n            })\n    return entries\n\ndef categorize_commit(message: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Categorize commit based on conventional commits\"\"\"\n    msg = message.lower()\n    if any(kw in msg for kw in [\"feat\", \"add\", \"new\", \"implement\"]):\n        return \"Features\"\n    elif any(kw in msg for kw in [\"fix\", \"bug\", \"patch\", \"resolve\"]):\n        return \"Bug Fixes\"\n    elif any(kw in msg for kw in [\"docs\", \"doc\", \"readme\", \"comment\"]):\n        return \"Documentation\"\n    elif any(kw in msg for kw in [\"refactor\", \"restructure\", \"clean\"]):\n        return \"Refactoring\"\n    elif any(kw in msg for kw in [\"test\", \"spec\"]):\n        return \"Tests\"\n    elif any(kw in msg for kw in [\"chore\", \"build\", \"ci\", \"deploy\"]):\n        return \"Chores\"\n    else:\n        return \"Other\"\n\ndef generate_markdown(entries: List[Dict]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Generate Markdown CHANGELOG\"\"\"\n    lines = [\"# Changelog\", \"\"]\n    \n    # Group by date\n    current_date = None\n    for entry in entries:\n        if entry[\"date\"] != current_date:\n            current_date = entry[\"date\"]\n            lines.append(f\"## [{current_date}]\")\n            lines.append(\"\")\n        \n        category = categorize_commit(entry[\"message\"])\n        short_hash = entry[\"hash\"][:7]\n        lines.append(f\"- **{category}**: {entry['message']} ([`{short_hash}`](https://github.com/owner/repo/commit/{entry['hash']})) - @{entry['author']}\")\n    \n    lines.append(\"\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\ndef generate_json(entries: List[Dict]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Generate JSON CHANGELOG\"\"\"\n    return json.dumps({\n        \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n        \"generated_at\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n        \"entries\": entries\n    }, indent=2)\n\ndef generate_text(entries: List[Dict]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Generate plain text CHANGELOG\"\"\"\n    lines = [\"CHANGELOG\", \"=\" * 50, \"\"]\n    for entry in entries:\n        lines.append(f\"[{entry['date']}] {entry['message']} - @{entry['author']}\")\n    lines.append(\"\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Generate CHANGELOG from Git history\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--format\", choices=[\"markdown\", \"json\", \"text\"], default=\"markdown\", help=\"Output format\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", default=\"CHANGELOG.md\", help=\"Output file path\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=100, help=\"Number of commits to process\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    \n    print(f\"[INFO] Fetching last {args.limit} commits...\")\n    entries = get_git_log(args.limit)\n    \n    if not entries:\n        print(\"[ERROR] No commits found.\")\n        return\n    \n    print(f\"[INFO] Generating {args.format.upper()} changelog...\")\n    \n    if args.format == \"markdown\":\n        content = generate_markdown(entries)\n    elif args.format == \"json\":\n        content = generate_json(entries)\n    else:\n        content = generate_text(entries)\n    \n    with open(args.output, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(content)\n    \n    print(f\"[SUCCESS] Changelog saved to {args.output}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n#### 💡 Key Advantages\n- **Zero Dependencies**: Uses only Python standard library.\n- **Smart Categorization**: Auto-detects commit types using keywords.\n- **Flexible**: Easily extendable for custom formats.\n- **Ready to Use**: Just copy, paste, and run!\n\n#### 💳 Payment Details\n- **Bounty Amount**: $50 USD\n- **My Wallet (TRC20)**: `TRkExdpdCrevJyqkKhcQ1g33pJ9jJPhh9z`\n\n#### ✅ Next Steps\n1. Review the script code above.\n2. If you need additional formats or features, just let me know!\n3. Once approved, payment to the TRC20 address above.\n\nLooking forward to your feedback! 🚀\n","createdAt":"2026-03-31T09:32:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4161228283","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M74B6A5","author":{"login":"zicaiw625"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"大王指令：放弃该任务","createdAt":"2026-03-31T09:35:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4161249337","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M74CBws","author":{"login":"geldbert"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-31T09:41:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4161281068","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M74CfZE","author":{"login":"geldbert"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nI've submitted a PR with a CHANGELOG generator implementation: #349\n\nThe solution:\n- Bash script that parses conventional commits\n- Auto-categorizes into Added/Fixed/Changed/Removed/Docs\n- Keep a Changelog format with Semantic Versioning\n- Tested on 676 commits from a real repository\n- README with 3-step quick start","createdAt":"2026-03-31T09:57:12Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1#issuecomment-4161402436","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M74Ci0R","author":{"login":"ormealex"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-31T09:59:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":